<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices mixed, livestock eases mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices mixed, livestock eases mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish procurement wheat, beef and pork prices fell in February against January, while rye and milk prices rose, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said. POLISH FARM GOODS PRICES	 FEB 97    JAN 97    FEB 96</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>   in zlotys per 100 kg	   54.06     55.38    52.08</p>
<p>   month/month pct change	 -2.4	-2.9	 7.1</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change		  3.8	13.9	41.1</p>
<p>@RYE</p>
<p>   in zlotys per 100 kg	   41.25     40.82    29.77</p>
<p>   month/month pct change	  1.1	 0.7	 4.4</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change		 38.6	43.2	26.9</p>
<p>CATTLE</p>
<p>   in zlotys per kg		  2.57	2.61     2.64</p>
<p>   month/month pct change	 -1.4	-0.3	 1.3</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change		 -2.5	 0.1	27.6</p>
<p>PORK</p>
<p>   in zlotys per kg		  3.23	3.38     2.58</p>
<p>   month/month pct change	 -4.2	-0.3	 0.6</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change		 25.5	31.8	 0.4</p>
<p>@MILK</p>
<p>   in zlotys per litre	     0.57	0.57     0.51</p>
<p>   month/month pct change	  1.1	 1.7	 0.2</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change		 11.7	10.6	25.9</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
